Bundled model: src/deidflow/models/es-clinical-meddocan-1.json.gz
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The built-in Spanish clinical span tagger was trained by DeidFlow on the
training split of the SPACCC MEDDOCAN corpus, with its development split used
for epoch selection and calibration:

  SPACCC MEDDOCAN (Medical Document Anonymization corpus)
  Copyright 2019 Secretaria de Estado para el Avance Digital (SEAD), Plan TL
  https://github.com/PlanTL-GOB-ES/SPACCC_MEDDOCAN
  commit 783a6df385c975b328c99bcffb54196a9ba4078a
  Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes: the corpus gold labels were mapped to DeidFlow entity categories and
used to fit model weights. The model file contains numeric weights keyed by
hashed features; it does not contain the corpus text. No source text was
modified. MEDDOCAN contains synthetic personal data inserted into published
clinical case reports; it is not a collection of real patient records.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled model: src/deidflow/models/es-finance-gretel-1.json.gz
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The built-in Spanish financial span tagger was trained by DeidFlow on the
Spanish training file of:

  synthetic_pii_finance_multilingual, Gretel.ai
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/gretelai/synthetic_pii_finance_multilingual
  revision 7b844d16738527a04264f50214cb426a4cea0897
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Changes: the published PII labels were mapped to DeidFlow entity categories
and used to fit model weights; 10% of the training file (selected by a hash
of each document's text) was held out for epoch selection and calibration.
The model file contains numeric weights keyed by hashed features, not the
corpus text. The corpus is synthetic and contains no real customer data.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled model: src/deidflow/models/es-general-2.json.gz
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The built-in general Spanish span tagger was trained by DeidFlow on three
sources together: the MEDDOCAN training split (attribution and license above;
development split used for epoch selection), the Spanish training file of the
Gretel synthetic_pii_finance_multilingual corpus (attribution and license
above; same 10% text-hash holdout), and 5,000 documents from DeidFlow's own
synthetic multi-country generator (deidflow.benchmarks.synthetic_es, seed 1729),
whose names, companies and streets come from the Faker library's Spanish
locales (Faker 40.44.0, Copyright Daniele Faraglia and contributors, MIT
License, https://github.com/joke2k/faker). Template families used for
validation and testing were excluded from training.

Changes: gold labels were mapped to DeidFlow entity categories and used to fit
model weights. The model file contains numeric weights keyed by hashed
features, not the training text.

